% notation.sty -- notation macros.  These follow the TARGET PAPER, not the
% textbook's convenience (CLAUDE.md, Phase 4: "notation follows the target
% paper").  Where the paper departs from standard notation, say so in a
% footnote in the text rather than silently normalising it here.
%
% ASCII ONLY under tex/.
\ProvidesPackage{notation}

% notation-check.sh reads THIS file to build its list of what to police, and it
% can only police ZERO-ARGUMENT macros whose expansion is a fixed string of at
% least six characters.  A macro taking an argument (\Hilb[1] below) is never
% checked, so a hand-written expansion of it will not be caught -- keep those
% few and grep by hand when in doubt.

